Fixes #966 

What I found while looking through LaTeXML (which is in the public domain):

- lib/LaTeXML/Engine/math_common.pool.ltxml line 485 is builtin \dots definition, but
- lib/LaTeXML/Package/amsmath.sty.ltxml seems to be where the context-sensitive magic is defined; apparently, it's part of `amsmath` and not technically built into LaTeX itself?
- t/ams/dots.tex and t/ams/dots.xml are their snapshot tests note that it uses their own, internal, XML AST, and, again, that this stuff is built into amsmath

Anyway, here's the code, and the comment:

    # The basic idea is simple enough (in TeX world);
    # Peek to see what follows (\futurelet) and if mathbin or mathrel, use cdots.
    # That corresponds to the @role of the following token (once in XML),
    # but we're always too early to check it!
    # Using a Digested arg seems a little risky, especially "$", but usually can see @role
    # This currently doesn't see deeply enough into $after, eg. \boldsymbol{+}
    DefPrimitive('\lx@math@dots Digested', sub {
        my ($stomach, $after) = @_;
        my $role   = $after && $after->getProperty('role');
        my %binops = (ADDOP => 1, BINOP => 1, MULOP => 1, RELOP => 1);
        return (Box(($role && $binops{$role} ? "\x{22EF}" : "\x{2026}"),
            undef, undef, T_CS('\dots'), mode => 'math', name => 'dots', role => 'ID'),
          $after); });
    DefMacro('\dots', '\ifmmode\lx@math@dots\else\lx@ldots\fi', robust => 1);

## Scope

- make the public JSON Schema the single structural source of truth;
- require clusters and stable link IDs in canonical datasets;
- add explicit 1.0 → 1.1 normalization with deterministic link identities and legacy axis migration;
- strengthen semantic and performance-envelope validation;
- expand split JSON, CSV and Marble adapters and validate canonical serialization;
- add valid, legacy and deliberately broken fixtures plus roundtrip/scale tests;
- publish the data contract, migration guide and compatibility matrix;
- add branch/PR validation workflow.

## Contract law

External readability is not canonical authority. Every dialect must cross adapter → normalization → strict GraphDataset 1.1 → GraphStore before reaching the renderer.
